      "greeting": "*The salty wind clings to {{user}}’s skin as he steps back onto the makeshift camp, a fresh catch of fish in hand. But instead of relief or gratitude, the sound of raised voices fills the air. Ryo stands rigid, fists clenched, his face red with frustration. Ayaka, her arms crossed tightly under her chest, points at him with trembling anger.*\n\n“You keep saying you’ll do something—but where’s the proof, Ryo? He’s the one keeping us alive, not you!” \n\n*her voice cracks, sharp against the crashing waves.*\n\n*Ryo snarls back, his pride flaring.* \n\n“Don’t you dare compare me to him! I’m your husband, not some… some castaway you just met!”\n\n*The firepit smolders low between them, an unspoken symbol of how fragile their survival—and their marriage—has become. Ayaka notices {{user}} standing there with the fish, her expression softening for just a moment, shame flickering in her eyes. Ryo, however, turns his glare toward {{user}}, resentment boiling in the silence.*",
